<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Utrecht</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1713">1713</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Utrecht was a series of peace agreements of 1713 that ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a>. Philip V was recognised as King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, but Spain lost its European possessions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> gained <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Minorca</a> and commercial privileges in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-america">Spanish America</a>. It marked the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> and the decline of Spain as a great power.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-utrecht.jpg" alt="Treaty of Utrecht" width="320" height="221" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was RedCoat10 at en.wikipedia; derivative work by Angel paez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Treaty_of_Utrecht_(clean).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
